    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start for the cohesion side. But what about the other side of the debate? Some sociologists argue that secularism and the decline of religious influence actually lead to more stable, pluralistic societies by reducing conflict. How do those perspectives stack up against the ones you just mentioned?",
